{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Kiryat Arba.</b> Named for four giants who were there — Achiman, Sheshai, Talmai, and their father. Another interpretation: named for four couples who were buried there, man and wife — Adam and Eve, Abraham and Sarah, Isaac and Rebecca, Jacob and Leah (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And Abraham came.</b> From Be'er Sheva." "<b>To eulogize Sarah and to weep for her.</b> And the death of Sarah is juxtaposed to the binding of Isaac, because through the tidings of the binding — that her son had been readied for slaughter and was nearly not slaughtered — her soul flew from her and she died."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:00.114372684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}